 README.md               |  2 ++
 SECURITY.md             | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 biome.json              |  2 +-
 4 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 SECURITY.md

diff --git a/.pre-commit-config.yaml b/.pre-commit-config.yaml
index db34765..cdad67c 100644
--- a/.pre-commit-config.yaml
+++ b/.pre-commit-config.yaml
@@ -23,10 +23,10 @@ repos:
         args: [--fix]
       - id: ruff-format
   - repo: https://github.com/biomejs/pre-commit
-    rev: "v2.6.3"
+    rev: "v2.6.8"
     hooks:
       - id: biome-check
-        additional_dependencies: ["@biomejs/biome@2.6.3"]
+        additional_dependencies: ["@biomejs/biome@2.6.8"]
   - repo: local
     hooks:
       - id: card-js-syntax
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 5fe3ecd..0d73642 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@ Home Assistant queries the Xtream server itself, so it works even when the serve
 - Home Assistant 2025.6 or newer
 - An IPTV subscription with **Xtream Codes API** access (server URL, username and password), **or** a **Stalker / Ministra portal** (portal URL and a registered MAC address)
 
+> **Security note** — the Xtream Codes protocol sends the username and password in every URL (API calls, playlist, streams). With a provider URL in `http://`, they travel in clear on the network: prefer the provider's `https://` address when it has one. The integration keeps them on the Home Assistant side (only administrators can display them, they never reach the recorder or the notifications).
+
 ## Installation
 
 ### Via the Marketplace (recommended)
diff --git a/SECURITY.md b/SECURITY.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4c42e4e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SECURITY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Security policy
+
+## Reporting a vulnerability
+
+Please **do not open a public issue** for a security problem.
+
+Report it privately with GitHub's
+[private vulnerability reporting](https://github.com/juju35/ha-iptv/security/advisories/new)
+(Security tab → *Report a vulnerability*). Include what is affected, how to reproduce it and the
+version you use.
+
+You will get an answer within a few days. Once fixed, the fix ships in a release and the advisory
+is published with credit to the reporter, unless you prefer to stay anonymous.
+
+## Supported versions
+
+Only the latest release receives fixes. Update through the Home Assistant Marketplace.
